1
00:00:08,260 --> 00:00:15,240
A group of very cold tourists are sitting in a cafe in Old Quebec drinking hot coffee

2
00:00:15,240 --> 00:00:17,260
to try to warm up.

3
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:20,920
The temperature is 32 degrees below freezing.

4
00:00:22,180 --> 00:00:25,120
The windows are covered with steam from the heat inside.

5
00:00:26,060 --> 00:00:30,640
Outside, snow covers the streets and is piled up along the sidewalks.

6
00:00:31,660 --> 00:00:34,200
The music and lights of the Carnival continue,

7
00:00:34,880 --> 00:00:37,140
but after a whole day of watching parades,

8
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:40,280
riding in horse carriages and listening to the music,

9
00:00:40,640 --> 00:00:43,980
their feet are freezing and their noses are red.

10
00:00:55,050 --> 00:00:57,950
Everyone who comes must be prepared to keep moving,

11
00:00:57,950 --> 00:01:00,910
as it is too cold to stand and watch for long.

12
00:01:01,970 --> 00:01:07,070
Early in the morning, you can watch the snowboarding competitions on the hill overlooking the river.

13
00:01:08,150 --> 00:01:12,150
Competitors speed down the track and through the air as though they could fly.

14
00:01:31,690 --> 00:01:34,570
One of the favourite events is the dog-sled race,

15
00:01:34,970 --> 00:01:41,190
in which teams of about six husky dogs pull long sleds at great speeds along a snowy track.

16
00:01:42,250 --> 00:01:44,130
One person runs behind the sled,

17
00:01:44,130 --> 00:01:47,110
shouting to the dogs to encourage them.

18
00:01:47,410 --> 00:01:48,750
The sound of the dogs barking,

19
00:01:48,990 --> 00:01:54,470
the calls of the drivers and the shouts of the crowd make an exciting Northern experience.

20
00:01:55,610 --> 00:01:58,010
The dogs are beautiful strong animals,

21
00:01:58,010 --> 00:02:01,470
with long, thick fur and many with blue eyes.

22
00:02:13,930 --> 00:02:16,650
It is amazing how warm these ice houses can be!

23
00:02:18,250 --> 00:02:20,730
Late in the evening, you can go to the snow palace,

24
00:02:20,730 --> 00:02:22,510
where Bonhomme the snowman is king,

25
00:02:22,510 --> 00:02:23,630
and join the crowd.

26
00:02:24,610 --> 00:02:27,010
You can dance outside to the music of a band,

27
00:02:27,010 --> 00:02:31,710
who are all dressed in heavy clothes - even some of their instruments are dressed up

28
00:02:31,710 --> 00:02:32,350
for winter.

29
00:02:39,950 --> 00:02:44,370
You might join the snowmobile races - or maybe you should just sleep in!
